.Language=English,English
.PluginContents=Google Drive

@Contents
$ #Google Drive plugin#
 Shows your Google Drive as a Far Manager panel.

 Open it from the Disks menu (Alt+F1 / Alt+F2), the Plugins menu (F11)
or by typing #gdrive:# or #gdrive:Folder\Subfolder# on the command line.

 ^<wrap>#Keys#
 Enter        enter a folder; open a Google Doc/Sheet/Slides in the browser
 F3 / F4      view / edit a file (Google files: text or CSV export, see below)
 F5 / F6      copy / move files between Google Drive and a local panel;
              a dialog asks for the destination folder. When the other
              panel is also Google Drive the copy/move happens on Google's
              side: nothing is downloaded, Google Docs stay native, and a
              move keeps the item's ID, sharing, comments and history
              (Shift+F5/F6: current item only)
 F6 in Trash  restore the selected items to their original folder
 F7           create a folder on Google Drive
 F8           move to Trash (or delete permanently - see ~settings~@Config@);
              inside the Trash F8 deletes permanently
 Shift+F6     rename the current file or folder
 Alt+F7       search inside Google Drive (pseudo folders are not searched)
 Ctrl+Shift+0..9  save the current Drive folder as a folder shortcut,
 RightCtrl+0..9   jump back to it
 Ctrl+L       show account and storage information
 Esc          cancel a running transfer (asks for confirmation)

 ^<wrap>#Google Docs / Sheets / Slides#
 Native Google documents have no binary content, so they are exported
when copied. The export formats are chosen in ~settings~@Config@
(default: docx, xlsx, pptx, png). F6 exports them but leaves the
originals on Drive. F3/F4 show a plain-text/CSV export: for a Google Doc
the plugin asks for confirmation before the edited text replaces the
document; Sheets and Slides open read-only because only the first sheet /
the plain text is exported. Press Enter to open them in the browser.

 ^<wrap>#Errors during a transfer#
 When one item fails (export too large, no permission, network) the plugin
offers Retry, Skip, Skip all errors or Cancel instead of aborting the batch.

 ^<wrap>#Special folders#
 #Starred# lists the files and folders you starred in Google Drive.
 #Shared with me# lists files other people shared with you.
 #Shared drives# lists the shared drives you have access to; enter one to
browse it. The drives themselves cannot be renamed or deleted here.
 #Trash# lists items you trashed; folders inside show their contents.
Deleting there is permanent; F6 restores.

@Config
$ #Google Drive settings#
 #OAuth client ID / secret#
 Releases of the plugin ship with their own Google client, in which case
the fields can stay empty and you only have to press #Sign in#. To use your
own client instead (no "unverified app" warning, no shared user limit):
 1. Open https://console.cloud.google.com/ and create (or pick) a project.
 2. Enable the Drive API:
    https://console.cloud.google.com/apis/library/drive.googleapis.com
 3. Consent screen: https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/overview ->
    Get started -> app name + your e-mail -> Audience: External -> Create.
 4. Test users: https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/audience ->
    Add users -> your Gmail.
 5. Client: https://console.cloud.google.com/auth/clients -> Create client
    -> Application type: #Desktop app#. Copy the client ID and secret.
 6. Paste both into this dialog (Shift+Ins pastes) and press #Sign in#.

 #Signing in#
 Your browser opens Google's consent page. If Google says the app is not
verified, click #Advanced# and then #Go to ... (unsafe)#, then allow the
access. The sign-in link is also copied to the clipboard in case the
browser does not open. Tokens are stored, encrypted for your Windows user,
in %FARPROFILE%\PluginsData\GoogleDrive\config.json; #Sign out# removes
and revokes them.

 While a self-made consent screen is in Testing status the sign-in expires
after 7 days; click "Publish app" on the Audience page to avoid that.

 #Move deleted files to Trash#
 When on, F8 moves files to the Drive Trash. When off, F8 deletes them
permanently.

 #Export formats#
 Extensions used when Google documents are copied to a local disk:
 Docs      docx odt rtf pdf txt html epub md
 Sheets    xlsx ods csv tsv pdf
 Slides    pptx odp pdf txt
 Drawings  png jpg svg pdf

 ^<wrap>#Opening the panel#
 F11 -> Google Drive, or type gdrive: on the command line, or
F9 -> Left/Right -> Change drive. Alt+F1/Alt+F2 also work unless the
laptop F-keys need Fn.

 ~Contents~@Contents@
